Please do not add any of these details to your records if you do not already hold them.

1. Erasure (Article 17). Please erase all personal data you hold about me.

2. Objection (Article 21). I object to the processing of my personal data for direct marketing, including any profiling related to it, under Article 21(2). Under Article 21(3) you must stop processing it for those purposes. I also object under Article 21(1) to any other processing you carry out on the basis of legitimate interests, including profiling.

3. Recipients (Article 19). Please tell every recipient to whom you have disclosed my personal data about this erasure, and give me the name of each recipient.

4. Suppression only. You may keep the minimum information needed to make sure I am not contacted or added to your records again, such as a hashed email address. It must be used for that purpose and no other.

5. Time limit. Under Articles 12(3) and 12A you must respond without undue delay and in any event within one month of receiving this request. That means by {{ deadline }}.

6. Identity. If you have reasonable doubts about my identity you may ask for the information necessary to confirm it, under Article 12(6). Please ask only for what is reasonable and proportionate. A copy of a passport or driving licence should not be needed to stop marketing to me.

Please reply to this email address, quoting reference {{ ref }}.

Yours faithfully,

{{ sign_off }}
